docs {
  # Get Lucky Draw

  **Method:** `GET`
  **Endpoint:** `/api/v1/groups/{groupID}/draws/{drawID}`
  **Auth:** Bearer access token

  ## Description

  Returns current configuration and result. All active group members can read the same draft. can_edit is true only for its creator while DRAFT and the group is active; can_run is true for every active member while DRAFT and the group is active. Use the full returned candidates to render the wheel in array order. Result index is zero-based. total_weight is always 100 percent.

  All routes require a valid Bearer access token, an ACTIVE account and active membership in the specified group. Every active member can see the shared draft and completed results. Only the creator may edit; every active member may run. Group owners and admins do not override creator-only editing. An inactive group allows reads but rejects Create, Update and Run.

  A group has at most one non-deleted DRAFT. Completing it makes room for the next draft. There is no delete, cancel, reset or rerun-for-a-new-result route. A repeat Run returns the same stored result. Concurrent Create is guarded by a unique PostgreSQL index; Update and Run lock the same draw row.

  Candidates have type, value and weight. TEXT value is a trimmed non-empty string of at most 255 characters. USER value is a positive JSON integer user ID, not a group member ID. USER candidates must be active accounts and active group members when creating or editing. User IDs are stored without a name or avatar snapshot. Fetch current names and avatars from GET /api/v1/users/{userID}/profile; cache by user ID within the page. A deleted/inactive account returns USER_NOT_FOUND; show a placeholder. Leaving the group later does not change an already-saved option or its chance automatically.

  WEIGHTED requires a weight on each option: greater than 0, at most 100, at most two decimal places, with a total of exactly 100. Values are JSON numbers such as 12.50, not strings with a % sign. Strings, exponent notation and more than two decimal places are rejected during binding. EQUAL assigns uniform actual odds. Omit weights for EQUAL; if supplied, they must match the automatic display allocation. Display percentages use 0.01 increments and total 100 (three equal options display 33.34, 33.33, 33.33); random selection remains exactly uniform in EQUAL mode.

  Duplicate TEXT values are rejected after trimming/case normalization; duplicate USER IDs are rejected. Different users sharing a name remain separate options. TEXT and USER are separate namespaces. There must be 2 to 100 options. Percentages are calculated with integer hundredths internally.

  Set drawGroupId and drawId manually in the selected environment. These requests do not automatically overwrite IDs. Login/Refresh keep their existing token scripts. Run the migrations before starting this backend version.

  ## Request

  Authorization: Bearer <token>. Path IDs are positive BIGINT integers.

  No body is required.

  ## Response

  **`200 OK`**

  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "data": {
      "id": 10,
      "group_id": 1,
      "created_by_member_id": 3,
      "title": "Who pays for dinner?",
      "draw_type": "WEIGHTED",
      "candidate_count": 3,
      "status": "COMPLETED",
      "is_frozen": false,
      "can_edit": false,
      "can_run": false,
      "result": {
        "index": 1,
        "type": "USER",
        "value": 7,
        "weight": 50
      },
      "completed_at": "2026-11-14T12:00:00Z",
      "created_at": "2026-11-14T11:00:00Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-11-14T12:00:00Z",
      "candidates": [
        {
          "type": "USER",
          "value": 4,
          "weight": 30
        },
        {
          "type": "USER",
          "value": 7,
          "weight": 50
        },
        {
          "type": "TEXT",
          "value": "Guest of the group",
          "weight": 20
        }
      ],
      "total_weight": 100
    }
  }
  ```

  ## Errors

  | HTTP | code | error | When |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | 400 | `BAD_REQUEST` | `bad request payload or parameters` | Malformed JSON, invalid field type, malformed percentage, missing required field, invalid ID/pagination, empty update or invalid title. |
  | 400 | `DRAW_INVALID_TYPE` | `draw_type must be EQUAL or WEIGHTED` | The service receives an unsupported draw type; HTTP binding may reject it as BAD_REQUEST first. |
  | 400 | `DRAW_INVALID_CANDIDATES` | `provide 2 to 100 candidates of type TEXT with a non-empty string of at most 255 characters, or USER with a positive integer user ID` | Candidate count, value or type is invalid. HTTP binding may reject invalid count/type first. |
  | 400 | `DRAW_DUPLICATE_CANDIDATES` | `text options and user IDs must be unique within their candidate type` | Repeated normalized TEXT or USER ID. |
  | 400 | `DRAW_INVALID_PERCENTAGES` | `weighted chances must be greater than zero, have at most two decimal places and total exactly 100; equal chances are assigned automatically` | Missing weighted chances, out-of-range percentages, incorrect sum or incorrect supplied EQUAL weights. Malformed numeric syntax returns BAD_REQUEST first. |
  | 400 | `DRAW_CANDIDATE_NOT_MEMBER` | `user candidates must be active accounts and active members of this group` | A USER option is missing/deleted/inactive or not an active member when creating/editing. |
  | 401 | `MISSING_TOKEN` | `authorization token is missing` | No valid Bearer header. |
  | 401 | `TOKEN_INVALID` | `authorization token is invalid` | Invalid token or a refresh token used as access token. |
  | 401 | `TOKEN_EXPIRED` | `authorization token has expired` | Access token expired. |
  | 401 | `TOKEN_REVOKED` | `authorization token has been revoked` | Access token blacklisted. |
  | 403 | `USER_INACTIVE` | `user account is deactivated` | Caller account is inactive. |
  | 403 | `DRAW_FORBIDDEN` | `only active group members can access this lucky draw` | Caller is not an active member or has left the group. |
  | 403 | `DRAW_CREATOR_REQUIRED` | `only the lucky draw creator can perform this action` | A different member tries to edit. This does not restrict Run. |
  | 404 | `USER_NOT_FOUND` | `user not found` | Caller does not exist or is soft-deleted. |
  | 404 | `GROUP_NOT_FOUND` | `group not found` | Missing or soft-deleted group. |
  | 404 | `DRAW_NOT_FOUND` | `lucky draw not found` | Missing, soft-deleted or different-group draw ID. |
  | 409 | `DRAW_DRAFT_EXISTS` | `this group already has an unexecuted lucky draw` | Another draft already exists, including a concurrent Create. |
  | 409 | `DRAW_COMPLETED` | `a completed lucky draw cannot be edited` | Editing after execution, including losing an Update/Run race. |
  | 409 | `DRAW_GROUP_INACTIVE` | `lucky draws cannot be changed while the group is inactive` | Create, Update or Run on an inactive group, including repeating Run. |
  | 500 | `INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR` | `an internal server error occurred` | Storage, transaction, randomness or token-blacklist failure. |

  Errors use the standard envelope: {"success":false,"code":"DRAW_DRAFT_EXISTS","error":"this group already has an unexecuted lucky draw"}. Internal details are not returned.
}
